Rollback Gate: UNSAFE
base: v1.0.0 (1111111, tag)
head: HEAD (2222222)
2 UNSAFE, 2 RISKY, 2 SAFE notes

UNSAFE  RG-DB-002  User.name
  at prisma/migrations/20261110000000_cleanup/migration.sql:2
  Base uses column "User"."name": by default base's Prisma client selects every scalar column of a model, so every query on the model fails, not only the ones that use this field.
  fix: Retire the field first (@ignore it and stop writing it; make it nullable if it is required), then drop it one release later.

UNSAFE  RG-DB-021  20261111000000_typo
  at prisma/migrations/20261111000000_typo/migration.sql
  Postgres's parser rejects this migration at line 1: "syntax error at or near "ALTR"". Rollback Gate can't tell what it does to base.
  fix: Fix the SQL so Postgres's own parser accepts it.

RISKY  RG-DB-020  20261105000000_seed
  at prisma/migrations/20261105000000_seed/migration.sql
  Migration 20261105000000_seed was released in base and edited in head. Environments built from head's history now differ from production, which applied the old version.
  fix: Never edit or delete an applied migration: restore the released version and put the change in a new migration.

RISKY  RG-DB-019  Post
  at prisma/migrations/20261110000000_cleanup/migration.sql:3
  The DELETE removes rows from "Post", which base reads: base code that expects the deleted rows (lookups, seeds, references) fails or misbehaves.
  fix: Soft-delete, or delete in a later release once base no longer reads those rows.

SAFE notes:
  RG-DB-000  User_id_idx  prisma/migrations/20261110000000_cleanup/migration.sql:1  A non-unique index doesn't change what base can read or write.
  RG-DB-001  odd`|<b>*_name  prisma/migrations/20261110000000_cleanup/migration.sql:4  Base doesn't use table "odd`|<b>*_name" (no model maps to it, or it's @@ignore), so dropping it can't break base.
